 I  host it for six months and then I stop  but at the very least I just kind of  want to evolve that product basically  and that's exciting to me they were  going to have the three male hosts just  rotate between each other while they did  like a search to find someone else so  again I want to say this wasn't  something that they were just like Ilana  you do this so that brings me to my next  point what do I actually do it IGN but  anyone who doesn't watch those videos or  like it doesn't pay attention IG and I  thought I would just kind of tell you  what my job actually is I am a producer  I was hired as a writer and then  ultimately recognized the value of  having a producer skill set so wanted to  start doing that more often what being a  producer in this role actually means is  coming up with  something whether it's a series or just  a one-off video and then seeing it be  executed for example last week we had  the Paris games week conference I had to  go to an event I asked our host max if  he could write a script about his  opinions on the loss of his pop didn't  ask him what opinion to give was just  kind of like I want to know what your  opinion on this is he wrote a script I  edited the hell out of that script I  submitted a request to basically our  video system to make sure it would get  filmed it was filmed I requested out for  the thumbnail I worked on the headline  and then I worked on making a written  version of it alongside Max and like  really fleshing that out I oversaw the  Edit I asked the editor to make changes  to the video and then we publish it I  host two weekly podcasts a Playstation  and our xbox show I'm not on all of them  every week but that is a big part of my  job there's a lot about live streams I  hosted the one for Paris games week but  I also just do like actual game play  live streams pretty often I don't  necessarily know what I'm going to do  those until like the day before  sometimes but I do do this quite a bit I  have a science segment that we've just  kind of started off to try and get off  the ground for like two months now on  our weekly talk show up at noon where I  just talk about science stuff very  excited about that one it's like it just  any excuse to me to talk about science  and it's great I produce two Let's Plays  a week for the PlayStation and Xbox  channels that we have which is  youtube.com slash IGMP on for the  PlayStation one and you should come  watch our channel locked for the Xbox  one again that means I come up with what  game we play I come up with who plays  the game I make sure that it's scheduled  and make sure the Edit gets done for the  beyond ones I edit all of them as well  and I just want to say I'm very proud of  those videos we record for an hour it  usually takes me three times the length  of the video to edit so those videos in  theory take four hours to make and I  make them every week and I edit from an  hour down to like 12 minutes and I edit  like dumb photoshop's into there and  stupid music I just  I'm very very proud of those videos  everyone I first started doing them  someone would be like ooh Alana's gonna  be mad about that at it because I do  like a zoom on my face looking very  unattractive and be like actually I was  the one who edited this and I produce a  weekly a Q&amp;A segment on the PlayStation  channel as well which is called  rapid-fire but that's basically just my  excuse of trying to get an IGN off-topic  podcast launched I've been wanting to do  that since I started and this is like  the perfect way to do it I also  sometimes help to write news and I still  try to put together cosplay galleries  when I can I also orchestrate pretty  much all of our unboxings meaning that I  get the product I unbox a lot of the  product but for the most part it's like  me talking to piada like get these  things in sometimes we put them on up at  noon and then I also do a lot of our  events coverage so I go to a lot of PAX  East PSX those are 